 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "Sri Lankan PID registry paper that describes two LAD-I siblings with stated features: 'Two siblings had leucocyte adhesion deficiency type 1(LAD type 1, with delayed separation of the umbilical cord, necrotic skin ulcers with minimal pus, high neutrophil counts'.",
 "method_note": "Written by hand (small Python script only assembled the JSON). The two LAD-I patients have no labels and no individual distinguishing detail, so they are 'unnamed person 1' and 'unnamed person 2' (rule 6); every value is from statements about the named pair ('Two siblings had ... LAD type 1, with ...'), applied to both and recorded as 'stated for this individual'. Sex female for both comes from Table 2 (LAD-I row: M 0, F 02). Table 2 also puts both in the '< 1 year' age column, but the paper does not say which age (diagnosis, onset or at study) the table uses, so ages are left not reported. Diagnosis was by CD18 flow cytometry; no ITGB2 genetic testing or variant is reported, so the variants table is empty. 'minimal pus' was recorded as an observed feature but the checklist item 'absence of pus formation' was left not reported (minimal is not absent); 'skin or soft tissue infections' was left not reported because the ulcers are not called infections. Table 1 counts (e.g. 'Delayed separation (> 4 weeks) of umbilical cord | 2 (0.2)', 'Gingivitis, oral ulcers/aphthae | 0') are referral-cohort counts without names and were not used. cohort_size_as_stated = 942 patients investigated (73 diagnosed with a PID). cites_prior_report_of_same_patients refers to the cohort's CD40-deficiency patient [26], not to the LAD-I siblings. Ethnicity/country 'Sri Lanka' comes from the cohort-wide referral statement. No contradictions found.",
